<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Surawisesa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned <a href="/years/1521">1521</a>–<a href="/years/1535">1535</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Surawisesa was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> from 1521 to about 1535, the son and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-baduga-maharaja">Sri Baduga Maharaja</a>. He sought Portuguese help against the rising Muslim sultanates, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banten">Banten</a> and the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-kelapa">Sunda Kalapa</a> fell to forces from Demak and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirebon">Cirebon</a> in the 1520s. He set up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batutulis-inscription">Batutulis inscription</a> of 1533 in honour of his father, and Sundanese tradition credits him with many battles in defence of the kingdom.</p></div>
